===
title: Kompat
---
<<if get_flag_uncheck("will")>>
	KomPat requires the password. 
	-> Insert his old password.
		Luckily enough he hasn't changed it since you moved.
		You quickly download the will from his personal K-Log.
	<<if set_flag("will")>><<endif>>
<<elseif true>>
	The old KomPat faintly glow.
	He didn't even install Orbit.
	Dad: Why would I install that, what am I a kid?
<<endif>>
===
title: Sleep
---
<<if get_flag("gotExtension")>>
	You managed to get the extension, today was very tough.
	You should close your eyes and rest, it's gonna be a long week.
	-> Go to bed.

	-> No. It's too early to sleep.
<<elseif true>>
	You managed to enter the workshop, today is not treating you very well.
	Should you go to bed? 
	Dad: You know if you do, you're not gonna be able to get the extension for my funeral, right?
	-> Go to bed.
	<<if trigger_end_of_game("You fall asleep, and wake up the morning after with the horrible awareness that something happen. You know your dad took his flight... alone.", true)>><<endif>>
	-> No. It's too early to sleep.
<<endif>>
===
title: cactus_office
color: green
position: -273,60
---
How is this cactus even alive!
In this enviroment?
In this economy?
There doesn't even seem to be proper light for it.
-> Maybe it's fake...
	Cheep polimare mold, but suprisingly convincing.
-> Maybe it's special...
	They water it with sunshine and kisses. I wonder what chem cocktail is keeping it alive.
===

title: bookShelf_office
color: green
position: -273,58
---
These are all just records... what a boring library to have.
-> Maybe I can still find something interesting?
	After careful analysis of the bookshelves, you conclude that there is in fact nothing interesting in there.
-> Nothing to see here.
===

